Article 2 (Duties of the Committee)
(1) The Committee shall deliberate on the following matters, present its findings to persons authorized to request disciplinary action under the subparagraphs of Article 7 (1) of the Judicial Disciplinary Act or persons authorized to request disciplinary resolutions under Article 96 (1) of the Rules on Court Officials (hereinafter collectively referred to as "persons authorized to request disciplinary action, etc."), the Minister of the National Court Administration, or the Ethics Inspector General of the Supreme Court, and recommend necessary measures: <Amended on January 29, 2021; August 29, 2024>
1. Matters concerning the necessity of commencing investigations into major audit cases, methods and results of investigations, and subsequent measures;
2. Matters concerning the handling by the Office of the Ethics Inspector General of the Supreme Court of complaints and petitions against judges (excluding simple matters such as dissatisfaction with the outcome of a trial);
3. Matters concerning standards and procedures for investigating misconduct;
4. Matters concerning plans and results of general administrative audits, accounting audits (excluding routine audits), and special audits conducted by the Ethics Inspector General.
(2) The term "major audit case" means a case falling under any of the following: <Amended on January 29, 2021>
1. An audit case involving serious duty-related misconduct, such as receipt of money or entertainment, embezzlement of public funds, or sexual offenses, by a judge or a court official of Grade V or higher;
2. Other audit cases involving misconduct attracting public attention, including media coverage, that have been designated for deliberation by persons authorized to request disciplinary action, etc., the Minister of the National Court Administration, or the Ethics Inspector General of the Supreme Court.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a case referred by the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court to the Supreme Court Public Officials Ethics Committee pursuant to subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Rules on the Authority of the Supreme Court Public Officials Ethics Committee shall be excluded from the Committee's deliberation.
